      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let the four positive integers be $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$\nWe can write the given information as:\n\\[a \\equiv 2 \\pmod{11},\\]\n\\[b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11},\\]\n\\[c \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11},\\]\n\\[d \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}.\\]\n\nWe want to find the remainder when $a + b + c + d$ is divided by $11$.\nWe can rewrite the sum as:\n\\[a + b + c + d \\equiv 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 \\pmod{11}.\\]\n\nAdding the remainders, we get:\n\\[2 + 4 + 6 + 8 = 20.\\]\n\nFinally, we find the remainder when $20$ is divided by $11$:\n\\[20 \\equiv \\boxed{9} \\pmod{11}.\\]\n\nThe answer is: 9",
