      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given four positive integers \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) that give remainders 2, 4, 6, and 8 respectively when divided by 11, we can express these integers in the form:\n\\[a = 11k_1 + 2,\\]\n\\[b = 11k_2 + 4,\\]\n\\[c = 11k_3 + 6,\\]\n\\[d = 11k_4 + 8,\\]\nfor some integers \\(k_1, k_2, k_3,\\) and \\(k_4\\). The sum of these integers is:\n\\[a + b + c + d = (11k_1 + 2) + (11k_2 + 4) + (11k_3 + 6) + (11k_4 + 8).\\]\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\\[a + b + c + d = 11(k_1 + k_2 + k_3 + k_4) + 20.\\]\nThis means that \\(a + b + c + d\\) leaves a remainder of 20 when divided by 11. To find the remainder when this sum is divided by 11, we compute:\n\\[20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 9.\\]\nTherefore, the remainder when \\(a + b + c + d\\) is divided by 11 is \\(9\\). Hence, the final answer is:\n\\[\\boxed{9}.\\]",
